One kind of cell (decision NBUI.5): plain text plus three boxes, made only by the box keys (Ctrl+2 square root,
Ctrl+/ fraction, Ctrl+6 power). A plain code cell takes boxes at its first box key; its text is then canonical box
text (4.4) and `--- boxes` gives the tree with the caret (`▮`) or selection in the box notation. When the last box
goes the cell is plain text again.

=== Ctrl+/ makes a fraction of the operand before the caret (a `*` joins a box and a name, NBB.14)
--- before
#% cell
1+x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "Q" Ctrl+Space "Z"
--- after
#% cell typeset
1+((x)/(Q))*Z▮
--- boxes
1+(x/Q)*Z▮

=== Ctrl+/ on a selection makes it the numerator
--- before
#% cell
⟦1+x⟧
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "2"
--- boxes
(1+x/2▮)

=== Ctrl+6 and Ctrl+^ make a superscript
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+6 "2" Ctrl+Space "+y" Ctrl+^ "n"
--- after
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))+((y)^(n))▮
--- boxes
(x^2)+(y^n▮)

=== Ctrl+2 and Ctrl+@ insert a square root
--- before
#% cell
1+▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "x" Ctrl+Space "+" Ctrl+@ "y"
--- after
#% cell typeset
1+((sqrt(x)))+((sqrt(y)))▮
--- boxes
1+√(x)+√(y▮)

=== Tab goes to the next placeholder, Shift+Tab to the previous
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ Tab "B" Shift+Tab
--- boxes
(⟦□⟧/B)

=== Esc name Esc inserts a Greek letter
--- before
#% cell
((x)^(2))▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ Esc "alpha" Esc
--- boxes
((x^2)/α▮)

=== Up moves from the denominator to the numerator
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "a" Up "z"
--- boxes
(xz▮/a)

=== Left past the start goes to the insertion point before the cell
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "a" Left Left Left Left Left
--- after
‖
#% cell typeset
((x)/(a))
--- boxes
none

=== Right past the end goes to the insertion point after the cell
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+^ "2" Right Right
--- after
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))
‖
--- boxes
none

=== Backspace in boxes
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "ab" Backspace
--- boxes
(x/a▮)

=== undo goes back to the text before the structure
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "y" Ctrl+Z Ctrl+Z
--- after
#% cell
x▮

=== implicit multiplication stays visible
--- before
#% cell
a▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "b"
--- boxes
a*√(b▮)

=== Ctrl+Shift+N on input that does not parse beeps and changes nothing
--- before
#% cell
f(▮
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+N
--- after
#% cell
f(▮

=== evaluating a typeset cell sends its canonical text
--- before
#% cell
6▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "3" Shift+Enter
--- after
#% cell label=1 typeset
((6)/(3))
#% output n=1
#= ((6)/(3))
‖

=== structure keys in a Text cell do nothing
--- before
#% text
# a▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/
--- after
#% text
# a▮
--- boxes
none

=== copy in boxes copies the plain text, which pastes back as linear text
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "y" Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Right Ctrl+V
--- boxes
(x/y)*x/y▮

=== undo puts the caret back where it was in the boxes (NB6.5)
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "ab" Up "c" Ctrl+Z
--- boxes
(x▮/ab)

=== redo puts the caret back after the edit
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "ab" Up "c" Ctrl+Z Ctrl+Y
--- boxes
(xc▮/ab)

=== undo of typing in a denominator keeps the caret in it
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "a" Ctrl+Z
--- boxes
(x/▮□)

=== Shift+Right out of a slot selects the box, Shift+Left back into it selects from the anchor again
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "ab" Left Shift+Right Shift+Right Shift+Left
--- boxes
(x/a⟦b⟧)

=== Shift+Right and Shift+Left after a box keep their anchor
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "a" Ctrl+Space "+y" Left Left Shift+Right Shift+Right Shift+Left
--- boxes
(x/a)⟦+⟧y

=== typed linear text stays linear: a/b, x^2 and sqrt(x) are just characters
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
"a/b + x^2 + sqrt(x)"
--- after
#% cell
a/b + x^2 + sqrt(x)▮
--- boxes
none

=== Ctrl+2 on a selection makes it the radicand, the caret at its end
--- before
#% cell
1+⟦x+y⟧
--- keys
Ctrl+2
--- boxes
1+√(x+y▮)

=== Up goes from the denominator to the numerator, Right leaves the box
--- before
#% cell
a▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "b" Up "c" Right Right Right "+1"
--- boxes
(ac/b)+1▮

=== Backspace at the start of a denominator unwraps the fraction into linear text
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "y" Left Backspace
--- after
#% cell
x/▮y
--- boxes
none

=== Backspace at the start of a radicand leaves the radicand; the cell is plain again
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "x+1" Home Backspace "!"
--- after
#% cell
!▮x+1
--- boxes
none

=== Shift+arrows select across a box; copying gives its plain text; typing replaces the selection
--- before
#% cell
a+b▮
--- keys
Ctrl+6 "2" Ctrl+Space "+c" Home Right Right Shift+Right Ctrl+C End "*" Ctrl+V Home Shift+Right "z"
--- boxes
z▮+(b^2)+c*b^2

=== a box key at an insertion point makes an Input cell with the box
--- before
‖
#% cell
x
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "8"
--- boxes
√(8▮)
